{"duration_api_ms":17955,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"19083195-cdcf-4205-a46c-ba443a565c24","total_cost_usd":0.227404,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34202,"cache_read_input_tokens":94910,"output_tokens":1869,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":523},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":34202},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":33372,"cache_creation_input_tokens":830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1869,"cacheReadInputTokens":94910,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34202,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.227404,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":523,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I updated the recovery middleware so a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` no longer logs a full \"panic recovered\" stack trace. The recovery tests and `go vet` pass. I haven't committed anything.\n\n**What changed (`recovery.go`):** the middleware now treats `http.ErrAbortHandler` (also when wrapped in another error) the same way it already treats a broken pipe or connection reset:\n- It logs a single line instead of a stack trace and request dump.\n- It records the error with `c.Error` and calls `c.Abort()`.\n- It doesn't call the 500 recovery handler, so it doesn't try to write to a connection that was deliberately aborted.\n\nThis error is how Go code (such as `httputil.ReverseProxy`) aborts a request on purpose, and Go's own HTTP server skips the stack trace for it.\n\n**Decision for you:** I kept that one-line log, as with broken pipes. If \"suppress\" should mean no log output at all, it's a small change; tell me and I'll make it.\n\n**Test (`recovery_test.go`):** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler`. It checks that the status code already written is kept, that the error message is logged, and that no \"panic recovered\" stack trace appears.","ttft_ms":2159,"type":"result","duration_ms":20935,"uuid":"8ec0374b-606c-4841-bac8-1868caa13e74","ttft_stream_ms":1020,"time_to_request_ms":172,"first_content_frame_ms":1020,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
